26	// Reopen loads layers in index order, stopping at the last complete, intact
27	// layer of one unbroken chain, then replays the WAL tail from that layer's
28	// cut. Any layer that is missing, truncated, checksum-bad, version-unknown or
29	// whose chain linkage is broken rejects that layer and every later one as a
30	// whole: recovery falls back to the previous usable layer, or to a from-WAL
31	// reopen when the base itself is unusable.
