54	// uint32 value length, the entry's commit sequence (uint64), the key, then the
55	// value. The base lists every live key exactly once; a delta lists only
56	// changed keys, with each key appearing at most once.
57	//
58	// The cut offset is measured in the WAL the chain is paired with. A checkpoint
59	// never modifies the WAL; compaction (the only WAL rewrite) first durably
60	// withdraws the chain and then re-establishes surviving layers against the
61	// replacement log before its rename becomes state, so a layer is never read
62	// against a different WAL than the one its cut describes.
